Source: homelab-blackbox-exporter
Section: net
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Jeff Gardner <mailmasker-api01@forge.name>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), perl (>= 5.40)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/permittivity2/homelab

Package: homelab-blackbox-exporter
Architecture: all
Depends: prometheus-blackbox-exporter
Recommends: homelab-agent, homelab-prometheus
Description: External (blackbox) probe wiring for the homelab-* ecosystem
 Wraps the Ubuntu-archive prometheus-blackbox-exporter on the fleet
 monitoring host. Ships the prober modules (http_public: public HTTPS
 vhosts, accepting redirects/auth-gated responses and always over TLS so
 cert expiry is measured; plus tcp/tcp_tls for raw mail ports) and the
 file_sd list of public vhosts to probe. homelab-prometheus' blackbox-http
 scrape job turns these into probe_success + probe_ssl_earliest_cert_expiry
 series -- the only "is it up from outside" + cert-expiry signal in the
 fleet. Advertises itself into the topology (kind: metrics-exporter, :9115).
